{
  "dom_id": "step-q328419",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+{75}^{∘})=-1\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx={a}^{∘}+n\\cdot {36}^{∘},\n$$\n\n \nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{36}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$",
  "worked_solution": "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+{75}^{∘} & ={135}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & ={135}^{∘}-{75}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 5x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={12}^{∘}+n\\cdot {36}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=12.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
